#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# fresnel_g

#% text
# `fresnel_g(z)` gives the Fresnel auxiliary function `g(z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `g(z)` is `(1/2 - fresnel_c(z))*cos(pi*z^2/2) + (1/2 - fresnel_s(z))*sin(pi*z^2/2)` (DLMF 7.2.11); it decays like `1/(pi^2*z^3)` for large `z`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values; `fresnel_g(0)` is 1/2.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
fresnel_g(0)
#% output
#= 1/2

#% cell
fresnel_g(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.06174085260964533

#% cell
fresnel_g(3.0)
#% output
#= 0.0036870010326249232

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The definition:

#% cell
fresnel_g(1.3) - ((0.5 - fresnel_c(1.3))*cos(pi*1.3^2/2) + (0.5 - fresnel_s(1.3))*sin(pi*1.3^2/2))
#% output
#= 0.0


#% text
# Large arguments:

#% cell
fresnel_g(10.0)
#% output
#= 0.00010130579448427637

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `fresnel_f`, `fresnel_s`, `fresnel_c`
